                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                        "entry_id": "c946a5aa-ab2b-32ee-9494-7925864a9668",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To load (cartridges for firearms) by hand."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42e5bc7f-ba7b-4d30-9ad2-3b6f1886db19",
                                "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                                "text": "He handloads his match ammunition. For long range he uses 49½ grains of 4064 powder, the Sierra Match King (boattail) bullet and Government (F.A. [Frankford Arsenal]) primers. How does he get Government primers? He pulls the bullets out of […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e9b97e4-1916-4ce9-b19e-9407f345dd4d",
                                "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                                "text": "You need what all of us could do with more of—off-season practice on running targets. That moral thought is all very fine if you live where jack rabbits skitter twelve months a year. The man from Butte or Boise can shoot moving-target rifle practice until he handloads or goes broke. But what of the chap from Binghamton, from a settled section […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ccd5767-3d08-4b84-a4e4-c7856bfff43f",
                                "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                                "text": "[…] in the .30-06. Of course he handloads, and American primers are easier to punch out than the foreign Berdan, a simple cup primer, for the anvil is formed in the case's primer pocket. Accuracy of the 6.5x55 and 6.5x.257 is about the same, he finds. The .30-06 […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ad417a3-940d-4281-af62-d52a6b7eb2cb",
                                "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                                "text": "[…] adequate power for the game in question, and as a matter of course he handloads. Instead of going to the 50,000-pounds-pressure levels he gets a case that's big enough to start with and doesn't need to be strained!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be975db0-9c5c-461b-91ed-3059b15d42b3",
                                "sense_id": "028bd53e-6d54-3a72-98fb-5fa0d80236b2",
                                "text": "He handloads his shells with less powder than factory loads have. The lighter load seems to kill a turkey just as quickly, but doesn't do as much damage to the meat."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a289a7c-3659-360a-8e18-bd77de676d26",
                        "entry_id": "c946a5aa-ab2b-32ee-9494-7925864a9668",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To load (a firearm, usually a pistol or rifle) by hand."
                        ],
